102         | NULL               | 200
101         | raj@test.com       | 100
103         | kumar@test.com     | -50
104         | invalid_email      | 300

Question
Using PySpark, identify records having:
* NULL customer ID
* NULL email
* Negative amount
* Invalid email format
* Duplicate records
Answer

from pyspark.sql.functions import (
    col, count, lit, regexp_extract
)

invalid = df.filter(
    col("customer_id").isNull() |
    col("email").isNull() |
    (col("amount") < 0) |
    ~col("email").rlike(
        r"^[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\.[A-Za-z]{2,}$"
    )
)

duplicates = df.groupBy(
    "customer_id",
    "email",
    "amount"
).agg(
    count("*").alias("cnt")
).filter(
    col("cnt") > 1
)

